# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SENSITIVE FAMILY / FINANCIAL DATA — must never be tracked in git (SPEC-010)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These files contain kids' school login codes + student IDs + DOBs, medical/Rx
# detail, insurance member IDs, patient-portal logins, phone numbers, full
# balance sheet (net worth, account last-4s, IRA/401k/Roth balances), Monarch
# transaction data, and client-confidential consulting pipeline figures. Per
# CLAUDE.md + TRANSPARENCY §5 ("family/sensitive data never in git"), and because
# everything under portal/public/ is ALSO served as a PUBLIC static asset over
# HTTP (no Clerk gate — see src/proxy.ts protected-route matcher), these are a
# double leak: git history AND the live web.
#
# The canonical source for all of this is Notion + the sweeps/Monarch pipeline,
# which regenerate it at runtime — so git tracking adds leak risk with no durable
# value. Target architecture: chatbot KB loads from Notion at runtime (mirroring
# src/app/api/1915-south/research-feed/route.ts); the financial dashboard fetches
# from an authenticated API route instead of <script src="data.js">.
#
# NOTE: This block prevents FUTURE (re)commits of new files here. It does NOT
# untrack the 25 files already committed here — that requires `git rm --cached` +
# (optionally) a history purge, which are DESTRUCTIVE and gated on Brady's
# explicit confirm. See docs/investigations/family-data-degit-plan.md.
public/family/kb/
public/financial-assistant/data.js
public/financial-assistant/kb/

# Keep the safe, committed presentation shell + zeroed template tracked:
!public/financial-assistant/data.example.js
!public/financial-assistant/index.html
